Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to mm/page_alloc.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    "page" (only tmpfs's storage chunks are allocated in pages)   4 -> 1 KiB
so a small file in / costs 1 KiB of kernel heap instead of 4.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/mm/page_alloc.ad --label b/mm/page_alloc.ad mm/page_alloc.ad <copy>

--- a/mm/page_alloc.ad
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.ad
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 
 PA_SITE_NONE: uint64 = 0
 PA_SITE_TMPFS: uint64 = 18
-PAGE_SIZE: uint64 = 4096
+PAGE_SIZE: uint64 = 1024            # Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 4096 (tmpfs chunks)
 pa_site: uint64 = 0
 pa_pages_live: uint64 = 0
 
